While it builds, fix the build script Stage-BackendExe. Also potentially add API test to backend tests? There's no test for routes. Could add but not necessary.

Let's rewrite Stage-BackendExe robustly:

```powershell
function Stage-BackendExe {
    if (Test-Done 'BackendExe') { ... return }

    $py = ...
    ...
    $spec = "$ROOT/backend/Novabackend.spec"
    if (-not (Test-Path $spec)) { throw ... }

    Write-Ck "PyInstaller-freeze: backend/Novabackend.spec ..."
    Push-Location "$ROOT/backend"
    try {
        & $py -m PyInstaller $spec --noconfirm --distpath "$ROOT/backend/dist" --workpath "$ROOT/backend/build" 2>&1 | Out-String | Add-Content $LOG
        if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "PyInstaller faalde (exit $LASTEXITCODE). Zie log: $LOG" }
    } finally { Pop-Location }

    $exe = "$ROOT/backend/dist/novatts-backend.exe"
    ...
    Copy-Item $exe $destExe
    ...
}
```

Also remove the weird bundling bits (`.env.example` and sounddevice data) since the spec already bundles `.env.example` and sounddevice data. The current manual copies are wrong (copying to `$exe/../.env.example` = dist/.env.example, not into the onefile exe; pointless). Remove.

Also the `$VER` variable inside function is stale but not relevant.

Let's apply.

