Bug: `$startIdx = [int]$FromStage` will fail for named stages ('BackendExe' → cannot convert to int). Fix: support both name and numeric.

```powershell
if ($FromStage -ieq 'All') { $startIdx = 0 }
elseif ($FromStage -match '^\d+$') { $startIdx = [int]$FromStage - 1 }
else { $startIdx = [array]::IndexOf($allStages, $FromStage); if ($startIdx -lt 0) { throw ... } }
```

Wait the docs say `-FromStage 4` = starting from stage 4. With 1-based numbering, index = 3. The comment in code says "4 -> index 3". So implement 1-based for numbers. Currently it's 0-based, which is a bug. Fix.

Also update the SYNOPSIS line 14 referencing "patched config.py (fix E:\)" → stale.

